condition_name: Constipation
condition_slug: constipation
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A clinical condition characterized by infrequent bowel opening and/or passage of hard pellet-like stools.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[4]: Infrequent bowel openings,Hard stools,Flatulence,Abdominal discomfort
investigations[7]: Full blood counts,Stool microscopy,Serum electrolytes,Proctosigmoidoscopy/Colonoscopy,Barium enema,Serum hormonal levels e.g. Thyroid hormones,Abdominal x-rays
treatment:
  goals[3]: Identification of aetiology,Restore normal bowel motions,Treatment largely depends on the aetiology
  non_drug[6]: Avoid precipitants,High-fibre diet,Adequate fluid intake,Surgery,Hormonal therapy,Avoidance of offending drugs
  drug[3]: "Stimulant laxatives - Senna (7.5 mg tablet): Adult: 2 - 4 tablets at night; 6 - 12 years: 1 - 2 tablets at night/or morning; 12 - 18 years: 2 - 4 tablets at night",Bisacodyl tablets 10 mg orally at night,Bisacodyl suppositories 10 mg at night
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[5]: Faecal impaction,Rectal prolapse,Anal fissures,Haemorrhoids,Rectal bleeding
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null